srow(302, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU HAVE FINISHED TITHING" (26:12) — AT CHANUKAH? AN END IS SAID HERE AND AN END THERE (31:10): THERE A PILGRIMAGE FEAST, SO HERE — THE FEAST OF BOOTHS? "WHEN YOU HAVE FINISHED TITHING": THE FEAST AT WHICH THE TITHES ARE FINISHED — PASSOVER; HENCE: THE EVE OF THE LAST FESTIVAL DAY OF PASSOVER OF THE FOURTH AND SEVENTH YEARS WAS THE REMOVAL. "IN THE THIRD YEAR" — THE SEVENTH YEAR TOO LIABLE TO THE TITHE? "THE YEAR OF THE TITHE" — A YEAR LIABLE; THE SABBATICAL YEAR EXCLUDED. TWO TITHES IN IT? "THE YEAR OF THE TITHE" — ONE TITHE, NOT TWO. ONLY THE POOR TITHE? "THE TITHE OF YOUR PRODUCE" WIDENED. The head row of piska 302 ({SP_(302, 1, "יכול", "בחנכה")} "could it be at Chanukah?"; {SP_(302, 1, "רגל", "שהמעשרות", "כלים", "בו")} "the feast at which the tithes are finished"; {SP_(302, 1, "ערב", "יום", "טוב", "האחרון", "של", "פסח")} "the eve of the last festival day of Passover"; {SP_(302, 1, "יצאת", "שנת", "שבוע")} "the year of the week (the sabbatical) excluded"; {SP_(302, 1, "מעשר", "אחד", "נוהג", "בה")} "one tithe applies in it"): THE REMOVAL\'S CLOCK — Passover\'s last day of the fourth and seventh years (Maaser Sheni 5:6 inside the spine, by the verbal analogy of "end" with 31:10 — I2 — then corrected by the verse\'s own "finished"), THE SEVENTH YEAR EXEMPT, ONE TITHE (the poor\'s in place of the second), ALL TITHES REMOVED — the compile\'s clock and the tithe-kind parameters for 26:12, and 109:1-5\'s rows of chapter 14 the same teaching (REREAD there). Fresh.')
srow(303, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL GIVE IT TO THE LEVITE, THE STRANGER, THE ORPHAN AND THE WIDOW" — GIVE EACH HIS SHARE. The head row of the headless piska 303 ({SP_(303, 1, "תן", "לכל", "אחד", "ואחד", "לפי", "חלקו")} "give to each and every one according to his share"): THE DISTRIBUTION by share — the four recipients each his portion. Fresh.')
srow(303, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THEY SHALL EAT WITHIN YOUR GATES AND BE SATISFIED" — GIVE THEM ENOUGH TO SATISFY; HENCE: AT THE THRESHING FLOOR THEY GIVE THE POOR NO LESS THAN HALF A KAV OF WHEAT OR A KAV OF BARLEY — R. JUDAH; RABBI: HALF A KAV; "WITHIN YOUR GATES" — THEY DO NOT MAKE HIM LEAVE THE LAND FOR OUTSIDE THE LAND. ({SP_(303, 2, "תן", "להם", "כדי", "שבעם")} "give them enough to satisfy them"; {SP_(303, 2, "מחצי", "קב", "חטים", "או", "קב", "שעורים")} "than half a kav of wheat or a kav of barley"): THE MEASURE OF THE GIFT (Peah 8:5 inside the spine — half a kav / a kav, Rabbi\'s dissent) and THE PLACE within the land (110:1\'s parallel at chapter 14 named by the translator); the compile\'s parameters for 26:12. Fresh.')
srow(303, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'THEY SAID: THE FAMILY OF THE HOUSE OF NEVALTA WAS IN JERUSALEM, AND THE SAGES GAVE THEM SIX HUNDRED TALENTS OF SILVER, NOT WISHING TO MAKE THEM LEAVE JERUSALEM. ({SP_(303, 3, "משפחת", "בית", "נבלטה")} "the family of the house of Nevalta"; {SP_(303, 3, "שש", "מאות", "ככרי", "כסף")} "six hundred talents of silver"): THE CASE of the poor kept in the city — the "within your gates" rule\'s story (Tosefta Peah 4:11; the row cites no verse). Fresh.')
srow(303, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL SAY" (26:13) — IN ANY LANGUAGE. ({SP_(303, 4, "בכל", "לשון")} "in any language"): THE CONFESSION\'S LANGUAGE ANY — against the first-fruits\' holy tongue (301:1); Sotah 7:1 the answer sheet (the tithe\'s confession among the things said in any tongue). Fresh.')
srow(303, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD" — THIS IS THE CONFESSION OF THE TITHE. ({SP_(303, 5, "זה", "ודוי", "מעשר")} "this is the confession of the tithe"): the rite named. Fresh.')
srow(303, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"I HAVE REMOVED THE HOLY FROM THE HOUSE" — THIS IS SECOND TITHE AND FOURTH-YEAR FRUIT. ({SP_(303, 6, "זה", "מעשר", "שני", "ונטע", "רבעי")} "this is second tithe and fourth-year planting"): "THE HOLY" the second tithe and the fourth year\'s fruit (Leviticus 19:24\'s holiness) — Maaser Sheni 5:10\'s confession clause by clause begins. Fresh.')
