srow(303, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO THE STRANGER, THE ORPHAN AND THE WIDOW" — THIS IS THE POOR TITHE, GLEANINGS, THE FORGOTTEN SHEAF AND THE CORNER, THOUGH THEY DO NOT BAR THE CONFESSION. ({SP_(303, 8, "זה", "מעשר", "עני", "לקט", "שכחה", "ופאה")} "this is the poor tithe, gleanings, the forgotten sheaf and the corner"; {SP_(303, 8, "שאין", "מעכבים", "את", "הוידוי")} "that they do not bar the confession"): the poor\'s four gifts (24:19-21\'s three the sheaf, the olive, the vine — and Leviticus 19:9\'s corner) named in the confession without barring it. Fresh.')
srow(303, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"FROM THE HOUSE" — THIS IS THE DOUGH-OFFERING. ({SP_(303, 9, "זו", "חלה")} "this is the dough-offering"): the house the kneading\'s place (Numbers 15:20\'s due). Fresh.')
srow(303, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "FROM THE HOUSE" — ONCE YOU HAVE SEPARATED IT FROM THE HOUSE YOU NEED ATTEND TO IT NO FURTHER. ({SP_(303, 10, "כיון", "שהפרשתו", "מן", "הבית")} "once you have separated it from the house"): the removal complete at the separation. Fresh.')
