srow(303, 17, 'MATERIAL', f'"NOR GIVEN ANY OF IT FOR THE DEAD" — I HAVE NOT BOUGHT WITH IT A COFFIN AND SHROUDS FOR THE DEAD: R. ELIEZER; R. AKIVA SAID TO HIM: IF FOR THE DEAD, FOR THE LIVING TOO IT IS FORBIDDEN — WHY "FOR THE DEAD"? THAT I HAVE NOT EXCHANGED IT EVEN FOR A CLEAN THING. ({SP_(303, 17, "ארון", "ותכריכים", "למת")} "a coffin and shrouds for the dead"; {SP_(303, 17, "אם", "למת", "אף", "לחי", "אסור")} "if for the dead, for the living too it is forbidden"; {SP_(303, 17, "שלא", "החלפתיו", "אפלו", "בדבר", "טהור")} "that I have not exchanged it even for a clean thing"): THE DEAD\'S USE — R. Eliezer\'s coffin against R. Akiva\'s a fortiori (I1: the living the greater) reading it as the exchange (Maaser Sheni 5:12); a dispute inside the spine — the compile\'s two arms. Fresh.')
